00:26:45.000 --> 00:27:24.000
physical signature that shows up in an autopsy. Heat-induced death looks a lot like organ failure or just general decay. And so, understanding the context in which the body was found is key. To do that, the department employs 40 medical legal death investigators. They go out to scenes to collect information. Whether the air conditioner is working, whether they've got access to food, water, collecting information at the scene, those temperatures, other signs of risk factors that help our forensic pathologists to make the correct conclusion about what caused or contributed
死亡的因素做出正确的结论。去年夏天，约翰斯顿的调查员团队遇到的现场都很艰难。他们发现蜷缩在帐篷里、伸展在柏油路上、瘫倒在后院里，或者被困在空调坏掉、室内温度飙升至130华氏度（约54.4摄氏度）的房屋里的尸体。每个人都处于极限状态。办公室处理的尸体如此之多，以至于他们不得不紧急调来额外的冷藏拖车作为备用存储。

51
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:59.000
to the death. Last summer, the scenes that Johnston's team of investigators encountered were difficult. They found bodies curled up in tents, stretched out on the asphalt, slumped in backyards, or entombed in houses where the air conditioning had broken and the temperatures inside had soared to 130 degrees. Everyone was stretched to capacity. The office was dealing with so many bodies that they had to call in for extra refrigerated trailers for backup storage.
他们本可以引进更多病理学家，但根本没有。这看起来不是一份通过简单扩编就能解决的工作，你知道我的意思吗？你的技能太专业了，凤凰城周围可能不会有一堆临时的法医闲逛。确实，是的。如果我们有空缺，平均需要20个月才能填补。全国各地的所有办公室都在为此苦苦挣扎，并且已经持续了将近二十年。

